     Altered?  Yes.  Trinary option?  Not really.  There is a boolean option
(i.e., either on or off), and when that option is on there is another string
option to limit what classes of objects it applies to.  The default for the
latter is "all" so that it's compatible with previous versions.  Likewise,
if "Pickup" (without the "_Types" suffix) is used in a boolean fashion, it
is treated as "AutoPickup", which has the meaning of the old pickup option
(again for backwards compatibility, so existing configuration files and/or
environment settings aren't required to be updated).  The '@' command still
acts as a toggle; to dynamically change the list of types of interest, the
'O' command can be used.

     Another change is that the "Disclose" option takes an optional list of
values and a slightly revised version of the so-called "kill list" has been
added.  "noDisclose has the same meaning as before; "Disclose" without any
value means "all"; specific values are one or more of the following letters:
'i' for inventory, 'a' for attributes (aka intrinsics), 'v' or 'k' for list
summarizing vanquished monsters (i.e., killed, but not necessarily by the
player; any monsters killed by traps and/or each other are also counted),
and 'g' for list of genocided monster species.  The first two correspond to
the old disclosure items; there's presently no way to access the genocide
list during play.  The value of the "Disclose" option controls which things
will be prompted about when the game ends.



